  Draft, YM-000026; parent author session hairer-codex-existence-20261111.
  Pin <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Prose
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-global-row-prices.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:actual-global-row-prices>,
  <verbatim|prop:actual-global-row-prices>. Disjoint from limits author's
  Barge product/Signal/Pupil assembly.

  <section|Exact targets><label|exact-targets>

  Namespace <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.MarginalMultiplier3b1d>:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|credit>, <verbatim|kernelPrices>, <verbatim|credit_post>,
    <verbatim|kernel_post> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticBridge/MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Ground.lean>.
    Fixed Pt:Teller G, P:Patch, hp:P.Branches Pt.bind G. Constants
    \<eta\>\<gtr\>0,K\<geqslant\>1,u,v\<gtr\>0 before eventual x; forall S,T
    with S.patch=P, 100(1+radiusB x)\<leqslant\>coarse side, Pt.Funds S T;
    forall A,F,k,V with A.flags=RG.flags(temp x)V. The literal Rows.gram is
    Q=M^T M on active link coordinates; N=per(panels A F)Q and
    C=clouded(panels A F)Q. Credit has Pours Q,C,N rate0 K; Q,C PosDef and
    Gapped \<eta\>; Pours(N-Q^-1) rate0 (u<em|exp(-v>(radiusB x/60))).
    Natural division.

    <item><verbatim|SourceBounds.source_bound>,
    <verbatim|SourceBounds.move_bound> in
    <verbatim|.../MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Source.lean>: same uniform domain.
    Fixed r\<geqslant\>0; 0\<less\>d\<leqslant\>r<em|fiery; forall q,Y,i
    source\<leqslant\>Z>fiery; move Pours between down/front anchors at rate
    Pt.top.width/2. Source includes frozen displacements. No differentiated
    dependence of frozen inputs on V is needed.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Reused canonical proofs and actual
  specialization><label|reused-canonical-proofs-and-actual-specialization>

  <verbatim|sector-gram.tex> supplies selected-row coercivity and weighted
  row/column bounds from local predictor derivative and cut-path bounds.
  Active Q is restriction of its inactive-completed precision, so zero
  extension proves its floor; no fresh small-panel assumption.
  <verbatim|local-covariance.tex> proves weighted inverse decay uniformly for
  principal submatrices, varying-window column inverse bounds, residual QN-I,
  ordered N-Q^-1=Q^-1(QN-I), and symmetrized covariance floor. These proofs
  apply to actual panels without assuming Q or C is the bare/flat Gram.
  Source <verbatim|Ground.per_approx> follows this exact residual route;
  source <verbatim|credit_post> combines opaqueCost, Schur.windows and
  provides, and kernel_post applies boards.

  In namespace <verbatim|YM.Next.SectorChange>, source
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/SectorNext/GAUSSIAN_SECTOR_CHANGE/Chosen.lean>:
  <verbatim|points>, <verbatim|meeting>, <verbatim|panels>,
  <verbatim|meetings>, <verbatim|boards>, <verbatim|fog>,
  <verbatim|opaqueCost>. Panels require all pairs of coarse endpoints at
  distance\<leqslant\>B/20. Endpoints are within1 of parent anchor;
  B/60+2\<leqslant\>B/20 for B\<geqslant\>120 gives ball inclusion. No
  upper-radius estimate is used in the residual proof. Weighted norm counts
  include color/orientation/residue multiplicities before periodization.
  <verbatim|Wisps.written> in <verbatim|.../Wisps.lean> gives actual scalar
  move entry bound at rate width, combining local face derivative, path row
  bound and <verbatim|earned>. Anchor counting halves the rate.
  <verbatim|earned> in <verbatim|.../Author.lean> clears a fixed predictor
  neighbourhood and uses its actual original tags; no globally-small
  configuration is inferred from local smallness.

  <section|Selected background and source
  calculation><label|selected-background-and-source-calculation>

  <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.MarginalMultiplier3b1d.Background> in
  <verbatim|.../MARGINAL_MULTIPLIER_3B1D/Background.lean> (read in full):

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|safe>: no flag in cleared dome implies small plaquette
    chord.

    <item><verbatim|setback>, <verbatim|spun>: signed coarse gauge and
    parent-lifted fine gauge; reversal moves anchor by\<leqslant\>1 and
    inversion preserves chord.

    <item><verbatim|turned_face>: four-link chord bound in a local gauge.

    <item><verbatim|face_base>: each touched plaquette gets its own gauge;
    path row sums and direct term give C*fiery. Global guide estimates come
    from Work.E04.answer/Work.E03.answer with empty-store Plot (frees_plot),
    which does not assert the actual store is empty.

    <item><verbatim|bond_base>: local log chart at actual selected predictor,
    then <verbatim|YM.SectorNext.Remainder.Affine.bond_local> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/SectorNext/LARGE_FIELD_REMAINDERS/AffineBond.lean> at
    a=0. Bound is linear C*fiery, not a falsely quadratic base remainder.

    <item><verbatim|base_post>: face and bond cases, subtract the same guide.
  </itemize-minus>

  Canonical Ct base-stroke proof reused from warning-safety.tex, first
  subsection, with explicit actual selected-store/signed-channel
  correspondence. Its subsequent mean calculation is not used for the kernel
  estimates. Further gauge/path/guide/local predictor inputs reused from
  seed-tree-patch.tex, seed-guides.tex (especially guide-maximum),
  seed-unhit-comparison.tex, predictor-branch.tex, packet-annulus.tex. The
  new prose explicitly localizes every chart and preserves period-uniform
  constants; path target gauges need not be one common gauge because only
  norms are compared.

  <verbatim|SourceBounds.{settle_price,barrel_bound,bump_post,source_bound,move_bound}>
  in Source.lean (read in full): all fine directions, not merely active ones.
  barrel sums isometrically transported plaquette derivatives against
  absolute path coefficients; predictor uses earned and a fixed stencil
  cardinality. Frozen <verbatim|Rows.input> has norm\<leqslant\>2d via
  patched_small (else zero). Rows.source is selected restriction of
  base+bump, with fixed slip factor; projection to scalar color has
  norm\<leqslant\>1. Exact constant can be taken slip*(C_b+2rC_a)+1. No
  derivative of held Y is claimed. Read <verbatim|Rows.{faceKick,bump,restrict,source}>
  in <verbatim|.../GAUSSIAN_SECTOR_CHANGE/Affine.lean> and
  <verbatim|Rows.gram> in Remainder.lean.

  <section|Scope and checks><label|scope-and-checks>

  Proves the three literal global suppliers for the forthcoming all-Matched
  palette argument; does not replace Barge's Signal identity or Pupil's local
  Toned-to-sock estimate. No posed-reader comparison is used as a global
  bound. Constants/tails depend on fixed Teller and Patch (and r for source),
  before period/stores/tags/field/frozen displacement. Thresholds may be
  intersected because only finitely many are needed.

  Searched shared background notes for Gaussian/inverse/Schur results; reused
  existing canonical finite-matrix and gauge proofs, with no additional
  external theorem or literature shortcut. Scoped rg/sed/cat reads listed
  above; no Lean changes, Lean build or fresh axiom replay. Candidate not
  integrated; independent mathematical/source review, TeX build and rendering
  pending.

